A||||4||fierocd||86 se to GT||||5||
Z||000000||fierocd||04-01-2001||07:20 PM||||I have an 86 se V-6 and an 86 GT, I am looking to make one complete car.  I was wondering which would be easier, making the SE look like a GT(changing the back end), or changing engines from the SE to the GT.  The cars have the same options so it makes no difference for that <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">.||||reg||5
Z||000001||GoCartGuy||04-01-2001||11:28 PM||||I'd say swap body parts, alot easier than messin with the engine.  Fewer parts to lose/damage/connect wrong means easier job.  Just remember that what ever time you plan on this taking add another 50% to it.  True for all Fiero mods/fixes.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000002||sjp777||04-01-2001||11:30 PM||||You can change the body parts in a day with basic tools. Dropping engine cradles is a huge ordeal without a lift.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierocd||04-02-2001||03:28 PM||||what is the easiest way to switchit to the fastback. I have a Chilton's manual but it doesn't go into very much detail.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||04-02-2001||03:37 PM||||You may want to also look at the underbody and miles on both cars to decide.  Rust is common behind the trunk carpet in the outside corners.  Higher miles may equal worn suspension.  I would factor in the overall condition of the interior as well.  For resale value in the end, it might be better just to drop the good engine in the GT.  Just some things to keep in mind...||||reg||1
